            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3449,
              "end_index": 3506,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This is a standard part of every CVL and is not optional."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              15
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3735,
              "end_index": 3801,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "A final meeting of members (and creditors, if applicable) is held."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              15,
              10,
              7,
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3925,
              "end_index": 4002,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The company is then struck off the register and dissolved three months later."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4032,
              "end_index": 4211,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The duration of a Creditors' Voluntary Liquidation can vary significantly based on the complexity of the company's affairs, the number of creditors, and the nature of asset sales."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              10,
              14,
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4213,
              "end_index": 4395,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Pre-Liquidation Phase (Initial Steps):** The initial process to officially place the company into liquidation can be actioned relatively quickly, often within **1 to 4 weeks**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4396,
              "end_index": 4455,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Some firms can initiate the process in as little as 8 days."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4456,
              "end_index": 4603,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Formal (Post-Liquidation) Phase:** Once the liquidator is appointed, the full liquidation process typically spans between **6 to 18 months**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              10,
              13,
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4604,
              "end_index": 4773,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "However, in more complex cases, it can take **12 to 24 months or even longer** to complete all stages, including asset realisation, creditor claims, and final reporting."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              16
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4774,
              "end_index": 4892,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors' involvement is generally most significant during the early stages, typically within the first three months."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4894,
              "end_index": 5052,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "While there is no fixed legal time limit for the entire process, the initial appointment stage provides immediate structure and relief from creditor pressure."
            }
          }
        ],
